<div>
<h2>Tools and stack</h2>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:27%">Layer</th><th>Choice</th></tr>
<tr><td>Reasoning model</td><td>Claude Opus 5.5 (<code>claude-opus-5-5</code>): adaptive thinking, JSON-schema structured outputs, strict tool schemas, server-side refusal fallbacks. Swappable behind one wrapper.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Agent loop</td><td>Our own manual tool loop (handles <code>pause_turn</code>; parallel tool results). No framework lock-in, and every step is logged to the trace.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Search / retrieval</td><td>Anthropic server-side web search; our own fetcher with an on-disk cache; HTML/PDF to text (BeautifulSoup, pypdf); BM25 inside long filings; fuzzy quote grounding with exact numbers.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Public data</td><td>NSE/BSE Reg-30 filings · results releases, investor decks, transcripts, annual reports · SEC EDGAR 6-K/20-F for ADR issuers · Screener statements · openFDA recalls &amp; Drugs@FDA approvals · FDA Data Dashboard, warning letters, import alerts, Form 483 FOIA · Health Canada NOC · CGHS/NPPA orders · ClinicalTrials.gov v2 · news RSS (first-coverage dating). No paid data.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics</td><td>Python calculators (shares, growth, implied priors, required run-rate, decomposition); every derived number is a recorded calculation with its inputs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Output</td><td>Jinja2 + inline SVG (no JS libraries; works offline, light and dark), Chromium to PDF; <code>run.json</code> holds the full ledger and trace.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quality</td><td>25 pytest tests: calculators, verifier, grounding (rejects a quote with a changed number), parsers, the LLM loop against a fake client, and the generality guard.</td></tr>
</table>

